\import{fcap-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\tag{fcap}
\tag{spin}
\tag{clifford}

\taxon{Example}
\title{Rank one: matrix units and occupation}

\p{Let #{K} be a commutative ring in which #{2} is invertible, and consider
polarization data for which #{W=Ke} is free of rank one. Let #{e'\in W'} be
the dual vector, so #{B_Q(e,e')=1}. Following \ref{fcap-0027}, put
#{c=\varepsilon_e} and #{a=a_{e'}=\iota_{e'}}; the last expression uses the
legacy contraction notation. In the ordered basis #{(1,e)} of
#{S=\bigwedge W},

##{c=\begin{pmatrix}0&0\\1&0\end{pmatrix},
\qquad
a=\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\0&0\end{pmatrix}.}

Thus #{c^2=a^2=0}, #{ca+ac=I_2}, and

##{ac=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&0\end{pmatrix}=E_{00},
\quad a=E_{01},\quad c=E_{10},\quad
ca=\begin{pmatrix}0&0\\0&1\end{pmatrix}=E_{11}.}

These are all four matrix units of #{\operatorname{End}_K(S)}.}

\p{The product

##{N:=ca}

is the one-mode number operator: #{N(1)=0} and #{N(e)=e}. Centering its two
eigenvalues gives

##{H:=N-\tfrac12 I_2
=\begin{pmatrix}-\tfrac12&0\\0&\tfrac12\end{pmatrix}.}

In several modes, #{N_i=c_i a_i} tests whether the #{i}-th exterior
coordinate is occupied, and #{H_i=N_i-\frac12} is the diagonal operator used
in \ref{fcap-0025}.}

\p{Over his characteristic-not-two field, Meinrenken supplies the general
creation--contraction exterior model
\citet{Proposition 3.5, p. 57}{meinrenken2013clifford}
and the normal-ordered isomorphism onto the full endomorphism space
\citet{Remark 3.5 and (3.6), p. 60}{meinrenken2013clifford}. The four matrices
above are the direct rank-one specialization made here. The centered
occupation operator independently appears in the Fulton--Harris calculation
\citet{Proposition 20.15, proof, pp. 305--306}{fulton2004representation}.}

\p{The occupation identity for every exterior basis vector is
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.SpinPolarizationData.wedge_contract_dualVector_basis},
and the general finite-free statement that the Clifford action reaches every
endomorphism is
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.spinAction_surjective}. The displayed #{2\times2}
matrices and their labels #{E_{rs}} are a basis calculation, not separately
named formal declarations.}
